WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.267 --> 00:00:02.434
-You know why everyone's
in a good mood?

00:00:02.434 --> 00:00:03.501
I want to wish everyone

00:00:03.501 --> 00:00:04.534
a happy National Beer Day,
everybody.

00:00:04.534 --> 00:00:05.601
-Whoa!
-That's today.

00:00:05.601 --> 00:00:08.801
[ Cheers and applause ]
National --

00:00:08.801 --> 00:00:10.467
Today is National Beer Day,

00:00:10.467 --> 00:00:12.501
or as we called it growing up,
Father's Day.

00:00:12.501 --> 00:00:13.834
[ Laughter ]

00:00:13.834 --> 00:00:16.033
"Give me another one."

00:00:16.033 --> 00:00:19.267
Let's get to some important,
happy, and historic news.

00:00:19.267 --> 00:00:22.767
Today, the Senate officially
confirmed Ketanji Brown Jackson.

00:00:22.767 --> 00:00:24.267
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:24.267 --> 00:00:26.534
♪♪

00:00:26.534 --> 00:00:30.067
Making her the first Black woman
on the Supreme Court.

00:00:30.067 --> 00:00:31.868
Come on!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:31.868 --> 00:00:34.601
Yeah!

00:00:34.601 --> 00:00:36.567
It's great.

00:00:36.567 --> 00:00:39.100
That's right. She's going to be
Justice Jackson.

00:00:39.100 --> 00:00:40.567
Yeah,
when Disney heard that name,

00:00:40.567 --> 00:00:42.834
they immediately added her to
the Marvel Cinematic Universe.

00:00:42.834 --> 00:00:44.133
[ Laughter ]

00:00:44.133 --> 00:00:46.634
Yep, Jackson will now debate
the most important issues

00:00:46.634 --> 00:00:48.901
facing our country,
like freedom of speech,

00:00:48.901 --> 00:00:51.767
states' rights,
and "is it cake?"

00:00:51.767 --> 00:00:53.267
[ Laughter ]

00:00:53.267 --> 00:00:54.801
Oh, this is cool.
Jackson actually watched

00:00:54.801 --> 00:00:57.167
the Senate confirmation vote
live with President Biden

00:00:57.167 --> 00:00:58.200
at the White House.

00:00:58.200 --> 00:01:00.334
Here they are, here's a picture.
Yeah.

00:01:00.334 --> 00:01:01.834
-Aww.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:01.834 --> 00:01:03.501
Looks less like
a Supreme Court confirmation,

00:01:03.501 --> 00:01:05.133
more like a Zoom wedding.
Doesn't it, a little bit?

00:01:05.133 --> 00:01:06.767
Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:06.767 --> 00:01:08.801
It's also an exciting time
in the sports world,

00:01:08.801 --> 00:01:11.267
'cause it was opening day of
Major League Baseball season

00:01:11.267 --> 00:01:14.267
and the first day of
the Masters golf tournament.

00:01:14.267 --> 00:01:18.968
[ Cheers and applause ]
All today.

00:01:18.968 --> 00:01:20.434
Yep.
Baseball and golf --

00:01:20.434 --> 00:01:22.701
it's basically the Olympics
for napping in front of the TV.

00:01:22.701 --> 00:01:24.634
[ Laughter ]

00:01:24.634 --> 00:01:26.267
But the big story at the Masters

00:01:26.267 --> 00:01:29.200
is that Tiger Woods is back
and playing great.

00:01:29.200 --> 00:01:33.634
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:33.634 --> 00:01:35.701
How annoying is that
for everyone else?

00:01:35.701 --> 00:01:37.367
-Yeah.
-The guy misses 17 months,

00:01:37.367 --> 00:01:38.767
he comes back, he's like,
"Well, I guess I'll just go

00:01:38.767 --> 00:01:40.901
win the Masters, I don't know."
[ Laughter ]

00:01:40.901 --> 00:01:43.000
Well, some business news --
I read that Richard Branson

00:01:43.000 --> 00:01:45.601
wants to swap rockets
with Elon Musk.

00:01:45.601 --> 00:01:46.734
[ Laughter ]

00:01:46.734 --> 00:01:49.100
So that he can fly to space
with SpaceX,

00:01:49.100 --> 00:01:51.567
and Musk can fly
with Virgin Galactic.

00:01:51.567 --> 00:01:52.934
[ Laughter ]

00:01:52.934 --> 00:01:54.868
So I guess Kimmel and I
really started a trend, right?

00:01:54.868 --> 00:01:56.534
[ Laughter ]

00:01:56.534 --> 00:01:58.701
Usually when two guys want
to try out each other's rockets,

00:01:58.701 --> 00:02:01.534
we can't talk about it on TV.
-Hey! Oh!

00:02:01.534 --> 00:02:03.968
[ Laughter ]

00:02:03.968 --> 00:02:07.000
-Hey, I saw that the CEO
of Red Lobster has resigned

00:02:07.000 --> 00:02:09.901
after just eight months
on the job.

00:02:09.901 --> 00:02:12.033
Now Red Lobster
has to pick a new CEO

00:02:12.033 --> 00:02:13.634
out of the live CEO tank.

00:02:13.634 --> 00:02:15.734
[ Laughter ]

00:02:15.734 --> 00:02:18.501
"That one.
That one's perfect."

00:02:18.501 --> 00:02:19.868
It's odd.
Usually the only thing

00:02:19.868 --> 00:02:21.801
that hangs around Red Lobster
for eight months

00:02:21.801 --> 00:02:23.434
is the coconut shrimp.

00:02:23.434 --> 00:02:29.634
[ Laughter ]

00:02:29.634 --> 00:02:31.033
Oh, people
are talking about this.

00:02:31.033 --> 00:02:33.901
The FDA is looking into
complaints all over the country

00:02:33.901 --> 00:02:36.501
from people getting sick
from Lucky Charms.

00:02:36.501 --> 00:02:37.801
[ Audience "Oohs" ]

00:02:37.801 --> 00:02:39.567
The FDA was like, "Well,
here's your first problem --

00:02:39.567 --> 00:02:41.601
you're eating marshmallows
for breakfast, so..."

00:02:41.601 --> 00:02:43.601
[ Laughter ]

00:02:43.601 --> 00:02:45.067
So far, the symptoms are

00:02:45.067 --> 00:02:47.601
[ Irish accent ] "pink eyes,
green tongue, and yellow skin."

00:02:47.601 --> 00:02:48.968
[ Laughter ]

00:02:48.968 --> 00:02:50.200
[ Normal voice ]
Some TV news.

00:02:50.200 --> 00:02:51.968
A lot of people are talking
about Ken Burns'

00:02:51.968 --> 00:02:54.534
new Ben Franklin documentary
on PBS.

00:02:54.534 --> 00:02:57.334
Have you seen it?
He's made over 20 documentaries,

00:02:57.334 --> 00:02:59.133
but, I don't -- maybe he's
doing it for too long.

00:02:59.133 --> 00:03:00.434
I think he might be losing it.

00:03:00.434 --> 00:03:02.367
I just felt --
I feel like the -- something --

00:03:02.367 --> 00:03:03.701
The writing's off.
I don't know.

00:03:03.701 --> 00:03:05.234
Take a look at what I saw.

00:03:05.234 --> 00:03:10.267
♪♪

00:03:10.267 --> 00:03:11.834
-Mm. Hot.

00:03:11.834 --> 00:03:13.534
Oh!
John Adams.

00:03:13.534 --> 00:03:16.033
Would you like some tea?
-Don't mind if I brew?

00:03:16.033 --> 00:03:17.901
[ Both laugh ]

00:03:17.901 --> 00:03:19.901
[ Slide whistle plays ]

00:03:19.901 --> 00:03:21.501
-And by the way,
have you seen my kite?

00:03:21.501 --> 00:03:23.634
-As if. You're never
getting that thing back.

00:03:23.634 --> 00:03:25.334
-What about the electricity?

00:03:25.334 --> 00:03:27.200
-Benjamin Franklin,
I don't have all day.

00:03:27.200 --> 00:03:29.000
I have to go back
to see my family.

00:03:29.000 --> 00:03:31.601
-What family?
-Why, the Adams family.

00:03:31.601 --> 00:03:33.901
[ "Addams Family" theme plays ]

00:03:33.901 --> 00:03:35.968
That's my last name.

00:03:35.968 --> 00:03:38.534
♪♪

00:03:38.534 --> 00:03:41.334
[ Laughter ]
-Wow.

00:03:41.334 --> 00:03:43.901
[ Applause ]

00:03:43.901 --> 00:03:46.267
I concur.
-I found it odd.

00:03:46.267 --> 00:03:47.334
Well, this is interesting.

00:03:47.334 --> 00:03:48.968
Researchers in Japan
created a --

00:03:48.968 --> 00:03:52.434
[ Laughter ]

00:03:52.434 --> 00:03:54.868
What's the problem?
-I'm just -- I don't --

00:03:54.868 --> 00:03:57.133
[ Laughter ]

00:03:57.133 --> 00:03:59.367
I don't know what
that was supposed to be.

00:03:59.367 --> 00:04:00.501
[ Laughter ]

00:04:00.501 --> 00:04:01.801
-What do you think you saw?

00:04:01.801 --> 00:04:04.634
-I thought I saw...
-Yeah?

00:04:04.634 --> 00:04:06.567
-...Benjamin Franklin...
-Yeah.

00:04:06.567 --> 00:04:07.667
-Right?
-Hey, okay.

00:04:07.667 --> 00:04:09.501
-...John Adams...
-That's correct.

00:04:09.501 --> 00:04:11.968
-...chatting by a modern-day
coffee station.

00:04:11.968 --> 00:04:13.200
-Yeah, like a -- like a Keurig,
or something.

00:04:13.200 --> 00:04:15.100
-Right? They're drinking
in demitasse cups.

00:04:15.100 --> 00:04:18.067
-Yes.
-He drank his coffee --

00:04:18.067 --> 00:04:19.934
-He's like...
-First of all, it's so hot

00:04:19.934 --> 00:04:21.100
that he had to go,
"Ouch, ouch, ouch."

00:04:21.100 --> 00:04:22.734
-He said, "Hot."
-"Hot."

00:04:22.734 --> 00:04:26.534
And then John Adams drank it,
and his eyes went --

00:04:26.534 --> 00:04:28.100
whoop! -- like that.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:28.100 --> 00:04:29.934
-Yeah. It was a little --
-That was -- Ken Burns did that.

00:04:29.934 --> 00:04:31.601
-Ken Burns
apparently did that, yeah.

00:04:31.601 --> 00:04:33.534
-Wow! You're right --
the writing is off.

00:04:33.534 --> 00:04:34.701
-I just --
Something's off, right?

00:04:34.701 --> 00:04:36.100
-Yeah, something's off.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:36.100 --> 00:04:37.801
-Well, there's no actual footage
of Ben Franklin,

00:04:37.801 --> 00:04:39.033
so they had to re-create it.
-Yeah, right.

00:04:39.033 --> 00:04:40.167
-So I guess, let him --
let him improvise.

00:04:40.167 --> 00:04:41.367
-You know what?
That explains it all.

00:04:41.367 --> 00:04:42.801
You have to improvise.
'Cause you don't know.

00:04:42.801 --> 00:04:45.133
You weren't there.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:45.133 --> 00:04:46.167
-Well, this is interesting,
guys.

00:04:46.167 --> 00:04:47.367
I think you'll find this
interesting.

00:04:47.367 --> 00:04:50.601
In Japan, these researchers
created a robot

00:04:50.601 --> 00:04:52.367
that mastered
a pretty important task.

00:04:52.367 --> 00:04:54.167
Check this out.

00:05:00.567 --> 00:05:05.634
[ Laughter ]

00:05:05.634 --> 00:05:08.200
-It's great if you feel like
eating a banana next week.

00:05:08.200 --> 00:05:10.000
It really is.

00:05:10.000 --> 00:05:12.434
People wonder why it's taking
so long to beat COVID, you know?

00:05:12.434 --> 00:05:15.501
[ Laughter ]

00:05:15.501 --> 00:05:17.133
Well, listen to this.
A driver in Maine

00:05:17.133 --> 00:05:20.601
had to be rescued after she made
a wrong turn at a garbage dump

00:05:20.601 --> 00:05:23.234
and ended up
on top of a trash compacter.

00:05:23.234 --> 00:05:25.167
This is real.
Look at this.

00:05:25.167 --> 00:05:26.801
-Oh!
[ Audience "Oohs" ]

00:05:26.801 --> 00:05:29.100
-Yet another success story
for Apple Maps.

00:05:29.100 --> 00:05:30.467
[ Laughter ]

00:05:30.467 --> 00:05:32.334
Anyway, happy National Beer Day,
everyone.

00:05:32.334 --> 00:05:33.968
[ Cheers and applause ]

